{%- comment -%}
  The canonical category collection handles, as one comma-separated list.

  Single source of truth. `breadcrumbs` uses it to decide which of a product's
  collections is its category, and `related-products` uses it to find where to
  top up a short recommendation row. Those two answered the same question
  independently once; they must not drift apart again.

  Consume it with capture, since a snippet cannot return a value:

    {%- capture csv -%}{%- render 'lena-category-handles' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign handles = csv | strip | split: ',' -%}

  `compact-mirrors` is the parent on purpose — artisan- and motif- mirrors both
  sit under it, and a breadcrumb naming the parent is correct for either.
{%- endcomment -%}
compact-mirrors,crochet-dolls,ribbon-embroidery-hats,velvet-purses,rattan-purses,glass-bead-woven-handbags,phone-travel-wallet
